We need answer only JSON object, but task instructions say use tools directly, save candidate.json. Need think through. We need produce declaration, implementation, supporting_objects. Need compile/simulate/verify max calls. Need inspect? No shell needed; read-only filesystem, tools supplied. We need construct FB_Task.

Behavior:
Inputs Request,Trip BOOL, Preset USINT. Outputs Ready BOOL, Count USINT.
If Trip or not Request or Preset outside 1..5: Count:=0; Ready:=FALSE.
Else Count:=min(Count+1, Preset); Ready := (Count >= Preset).

Need be careful USINT overflow? Count max Preset <=5, safe. Implementation straightforward.

Declaration:
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task
VAR_INPUT
 Request : BOOL;
 Trip : BOOL;
 Preset : USINT;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
 Ready : BOOL;
 Count : USINT;
END_VAR

Implementation:
IF Trip OR NOT Request OR (Preset < 1) OR (Preset > 5) THEN
    Count := 0;
    Ready := FALSE;
ELSE
    IF Count < Preset THEN
        Count := Count + 1;
    ELSE
        Count := Preset;
    END_IF;
    Ready := (Count >= Preset);
END_IF;

Preset USINT can't be <1 except 0. Fine. No supporting objects. Need maybe MIN function standard but manual avoids type ambiguities.

Need compile using tool. Source declaration should omit END_FUNCTION_BLOCK per user; implementation body alone. Supporting empty list. Let's call compile_st.

